        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ed3964fd-d10e-5f3c-8e73-61e29f2d2efc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Juan Darién: A Carnival Mass, Frida\n- People: Elliot Goldenthal, Julie Taymor\n- Awards: Obie Award, Academy Award for Best Original Score\n- Places: Off-Broadway, Broadway\n- Topics: film scores, contemporary classical music\n\nFacts:\n- Elliot Goldenthal was born on May 2, 1954, and is an American composer of film scores and contemporary classical music.\n- Around 1988, Elliot Goldenthal first composed the Obie Award-winning score for Juan Darién: A Carnival Mass when the musical opened off-Broadway in a small former church.\n- In 1996, Elliot Goldenthal reworked and refined the score for Juan Darién: A Carnival Mass for the show's Broadway release.\n- In 2002, Elliot Goldenthal won the Academy Award for Best Original Score for Frida, a motion picture directed by his long-time partner Julie Taymor.",
